  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Community-based adaptation in South East Asia and Pacific Program</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This investment supports implementation of community-based adaptation programs in countries in Southeast Asia (including Cambodia, Laos, Philippines and Vietnam) and in the Pacific (including Fiji, Kiribati, Samoa, Solomon Islands, Tonga and Timor Leste). It is implemented by the Global Environment Facility&#x2019;s Small Grants Program through the United Nations Development Program, in collaboration with a network of national coordinating committees set up across Asia-Pacific. These committees seek and select funding proposals from local organisations and communities related to climate adaptation.</narrative>
  </description>
